Embedded React: keep an occluded translated node's paint record translated.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/scene/compositor.c,
engine/tests/rendering/CMakeLists.txt and the new
engine/tests/rendering/test_occluded_translate.c. Proposed upstream as pull
request #313.

An opaque node covering a damage rect buries the subtrees painted before it
whose cached prune flag says they hold no transform, but a clipping container
leaves its children's transforms out of that flag. A translated node inside
such a container (a header's sliding section pill, beside a spinner under an
opaque cover) was walked as occluded, which skipped its translate, so it
recorded its untranslated box as where it last painted. The next move erased
that box instead of the pixels it had painted and left pieces of the pill on
screen. The translate-only offset is now applied to occluded nodes too; the
transform capture is still skipped for them.

diff --git a/engine/scene/compositor.c b/engine/scene/compositor.c
index b57968d..e5ad8a0 100644
--- a/engine/scene/compositor.c
+++ b/engine/scene/compositor.c
@@ -2278,8 +2278,16 @@ static void render_tree(ERNode* n, bool parent_dirty, bool occluded, int transla
     const bool complex_xf = er_node_has_complex_transform(n);
 #endif
     /* An occluded node never captures a transform source: the scratch render would be thrown away,
-     * and the cull only ever occludes transform-free subtrees anyway (see the subtree_prunable gate). */
-    if (n->has_transform && !occluded)
+     * and the cull only ever occludes transform-free subtrees anyway (see the subtree_prunable gate).
+     * A translate is still applied: it is arithmetic, and it is where the node and its subtree record
+     * last_paint_rect. Burying is not as transform-free as that gate suggests, since a clipping
+     * container leaves its children's transforms out of its own flag; an occluded translated node
+     * that recorded its untranslated box made the next move erase that box and leave a trail. */
+#if ERUI_TRANSFORMS_FULL
+    if (n->has_transform && !(occluded && complex_xf))
+#else
+    if (n->has_transform)
+#endif
     {
 #if ERUI_3D_TRANSFORMS && ERUI_TRANSFORMS_FULL
         if (complex_xf && er_transform_is_3d(n))
